@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{eww-extras.el} extends EWW (Emacs Web Wowser)@comma{} the built-in Emacs web
browser@comma{} with capabilities for generating files from web pages@comma{} managing
readability mode@comma{} navigating URL hierarchies@comma{} and integrating with other
packages.  It depends on the @samp{paths} and @samp{el-patch} packages.

The most substantial feature is the ability to generate PDF and HTML
files from any URL using headless Chrome.  This requires Chrome to be
installed and uses copies of the user's Chrome profile data for
authentication@comma{} enabling downloads from sites that require login.  The
generated files are placed in the downloads directory and can optionally
trigger a callback function (e.g.@comma{} to attach the file to a Bib@TeX{}
entry).

The package also enhances EWW's readability mode.  By default@comma{} every
page rendered in EWW is automatically converted to its ``readable'' form
(stripping navigation@comma{} ads@comma{} and other clutter).  A file-backed exception
list allows excluding specific domains where readability mode produces
poor results.  Adding exceptions is a single command away.

For navigation@comma{} the package provides Vimium-style commands: editing the
current URL@comma{} opening kill ring content@comma{} and moving up or to the root of
the URL hierarchy.  It also provides commands for switching between EWW
and xwidget-webkit for different rendering needs.

Integration with other packages includes handling YouTube URLs via
@samp{elfeed-tube} (for transcript extraction) and @samp{mpv} (for video
playback)@comma{} and adding the current page to a bibliography via
@samp{zotra-extras}.

